  "reason": "The study uses simulation to assess uncertainty in NOAEL estimation and its application to clinical dose escalation. While it discusses the discrepancy between species and the risk of toxicity or under-dosing, it does not report a quantitative measure of agreement (e.g., concordance rate, PPV, sensitivity/specificity) between animal and human results. It focuses on the uncertainty and risk associated with the *application* of animal data rather than a direct statistical comparison of concordance."
